{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790195828,"nonce":"4Lvc02h0aGoA9lml8wdoD/psI4A=","message":"Generated GPU descriptors now expose constructors and setters through ordinary\nCaribou plugin classes. Constructors containing another descriptor are\ncorrectly classified as static constructors after `522d275`.\n\nDescriptor setters and constructors that take generated enums still expose the\nexisting Wren gap: Wren can read returned enums but cannot generally construct\nvalues such as `gpu.TextureFormat`, `gpu.AddressMode` or\n`gpu.TextureViewDimension`. Numeric substitutes were deliberately not added to\nthe public GPU API. Lossless Int64 behavior is unchanged.","files":null}]}